------------------------------------------------- MODULE StorageTrace --------------------------------------------------
\* Generated by `engramctl formal trace-to-tla` from a schema-v1 log of 6 events of Storage. Do not edit. TraceSpec
\* replays the events one per step through the operators of the specification (in a log that records states: through
\* Next, each step pinned to its logged state); the invariants of the configuration are checked on every state of every
\* replay. TraceNotDone is violated exactly when some execution has consumed the whole log, i.e. when the log is a
\* behaviour of the specification.
EXTENDS Storage, Naturals, Sequences, TLC

VARIABLE l

TraceEvents == <<
  [act |-> "Insert", par |-> <<1>>],
  [act |-> "Mark", par |-> <<1>>],
  [act |-> "EmbedRow", par |-> <<1, 1>>],
  [act |-> "IndexAdd", par |-> <<<<1, 1>>>>],
  [act |-> "Purge", par |-> <<1>>],
  [act |-> "AutoRepairDrop", par |-> <<<<1, 1>>>>]
>>

tvars == <<vars, l>>

TraceInit == Init /\ l = 1

TraceReplay ==
  /\ l <= Len(TraceEvents)
  /\ l' = l + 1
  /\ \/ FALSE
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "Insert" /\ Insert(TraceEvents[l].par[1])
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "Mark" /\ Mark(TraceEvents[l].par[1])
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "EmbedRow" /\ EmbedRow(TraceEvents[l].par[1], TraceEvents[l].par[2])
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "IndexAdd" /\ IndexAdd(TraceEvents[l].par[1])
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "Purge" /\ Purge(TraceEvents[l].par[1])
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "AutoRepairDrop" /\ AutoRepairDrop(TraceEvents[l].par[1])

\* One step after the last event, so that every state of the replay is checked against the invariants before
\* TraceNotDone can fail (TLC checks a state when it generates it).
TraceFinish == l = Len(TraceEvents) + 1 /\ l' = l + 1 /\ UNCHANGED vars

TraceNext == TraceReplay \/ TraceFinish

TraceSpec == TraceInit /\ [][TraceNext]_tvars

TraceNotDone == l <= Len(TraceEvents) + 1

========================================================================================================================
